meta {
  name: Space List Repos
  type: http
  seq: 159
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.listRepos?space=at://{{did}}/space/org.example.bucket/main&limit=100
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  space: at://{{did}}/space/org.example.bucket/main
  limit: 100
  ~cursor:
}

docs {
  The space host's writer set: every repo that has written into the space, with the rev and
  commit hash last reported for it. This is the sync boundary, not an access-control list —
  it enumerates writers, never readers, and a member who has only ever read is absent.

  For a repo hosted elsewhere the rev/hash come from that host's notifyWrite and may lag; the
  repo's own host is the source of truth. Syncers use this as the periodic sweep that heals
  anything the best-effort write notifications missed.

  Answered only by the space's authority. A space this server merely keeps repos in reads as
  400 SpaceNotFound — ask its authority instead. Auth: a space credential, or the authority's
  own session.
}
